# Cursor Rules for weisssrv

Production Proxmox homelab managed as Infrastructure as Code. The tech stack is
described once, in `CLAUDE.md` § Project Overview.

1. Read `CLAUDE.md` first — project overview, architecture, repo family, secrets
   and version management. It names the canonical source for everything owned
   elsewhere (`README.md` for the docs index, `docs/01-overview.md` for IPs,
   `docs/15-credential-rotation.md` for 1Password items, `ansible/README.md` for
   Ansible conventions, `task --list` for commands).
2. Then read `.claude/skills/weisssrv-development/SKILL.md` and the `references/`
   file for the change at hand. It is the single home of the workflow invariants
   (branch + MR, never push `main`, no secrets in git, Flux owns `kubernetes/`,
   single-sourced versions, roles change in weisssrv-lib), the pre-MR gates, and
   the change-type decision tree. Follow it rather than these notes.
